          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completion"} formal completion
          %h2#references References
          %p The concept originates with
          %ul
            %li#Bousfield79
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aldridge+Bousfield"}> Aldridge Bousfield
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The localization of spectra with respect to homology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.uio.no/studier/emner/matnat/math/MAT9580/v12/undervisningsmateriale/bousfield-topology-1979.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Ravenel84
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Ravenel"}> Douglas Ravenel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Localization with respect to certain periodic homology theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/mypapers/loc.pdf"} pdf
          %p The re-interpretation in terms of totalization of the cosimplicial spectrum is briefly mentioned in
          %ul
            %li#Hopkins99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"}> Mike Hopkins
              , section 4 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Complex oriented cohomology theories and the language of stacks
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/coctalos.pdf"} pdf
          %p and tacitly assumed in
          %ul
            %li#Lurie10
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chromatic+Homotopy+Theory"} Chromatic Homotopy Theory
              (2010) lecture 30:
              %em Localizations and the Adams-Novikov Spectral Sequence
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~lurie/252xnotes/Lecture30.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A proof of the equivalence of this re-interpretation appears in
          %ul
            %li#MathewNaumannNoel15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"}> Akhil Mathew
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niko+Naumann"} Niko Naumann
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Justin+Noel"} Justin Noel
              %em Nilpotence and descent in equivariant stable homotopy theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1507.06869"}> arXiv:1507.06869
              )
          %p See also
